# Store and check out text as LF, everywhere in this repository.
#
# site/.gitattributes has said this for the site since it was written, and the
# reason there was that git on Windows otherwise rewrites the working copy to
# CRLF, which is harmless for the served files but makes every one of them look
# modified on the next publish and buries real changes in noise.
#
# The rule needed to cover the whole repository, not just site/, and the two
# days it did not cost two debugging sessions:
#
#   2026-09-06  Restoring site/ to its declared format put seven page
#               generators into drift at once. They had all been writing CRLF
#               through Python's text mode on Windows and had only ever passed
#               because the checked-out tree had drifted to CRLF too and agreed
#               with them by accident. The bug was as old as the masking.
#
#   2026-09-07  bust_cache.py was still writing CRLF - it had been missed in
#               that sweep - and nothing caught it, because it happened to
#               stamp nothing for the rest of that session. The moment
#               style.css changed it rewrote every page in the site and flipped
#               the whole tree back. sync_img_dims.py, which used newline="",
#               then faithfully preserved the damage.
#
# The generators now all pass newline="\n" explicitly, which is the real fix;
# this file is the other half, so that a checkout cannot put the tree into a
# state where writing the declared format looks like drift.
#
# Never use newline="" in a generator that writes into the tree. It preserves
# whatever it finds, so it agrees with a drifted tree and hides exactly this.
# The exception is csv.writer, which requires newline="" and handles its own
# line terminator.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched. The heuristic behind text=auto is good but
# it is a heuristic, and these are the types actually tracked here.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.npz   binary
*.npy   binary
*.parquet binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.otf   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
